Plasmolysis reveals novel p33 localization
Given that the p33-assosciated vesicles were found situated between the plasma membrane and the cell wall, the GFP:p33 localization was next observed under the plasmolysis conditions to separate the plasma membrane from the cell wall. GFP:p33 strongly and consistently localized to the Hechtian strands, the linkers between the plasma membrane and the cell wall of plant cells (
Fig 8A
).
